§§ `Row 6 -- foodpanda and food delivery`

-- Ordered and paid in the app. NOT named `foodpanda`: since 2026-09-21 that
-- is a `Merchant` constructor in the domain module, and a third definition
-- exists in a card module, so the bare token is overloaded three ways and
-- resolves by type at each use site. That works until it does not, and the
-- line it would fail on -- a fixture name, an argument and a string literal
-- all reading "foodpanda" -- is one nobody would re-read. Renamed instead.
`S5 a foodpanda order` MEANS `S5 an online purchase at` "foodpanda" foodpanda 5814 45

-- [S5] "foodpanda / food delivery (MCC 5814) | DBS yuu (10, S$822)"
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 a foodpanda order`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `DBS yuu Visa` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 a foodpanda order`)'s `cap`'s `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 822
-- [S5] "Solitaire -- Dining (6, S$750, if cap room)"
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 a foodpanda order`)'s `miles per dollar` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (`the rate on` `UOB Lady's Solitaire` `S5 the cardholder` `S5 the month` `S5 a foodpanda order`)'s `cap`'s `bonus spend per month` EQUALS 750
