-- ===========================================================================
-- WHAT THE CHEAT SHEET SAYS THAT THIS DOMAIN CANNOT HOLD
--
-- Four claims were read off the sheet and are not asserted below. They are listed rather than dropped, because "not asserted" and
-- "asserted and passing" are not the same evidence, and a later reader
-- counting assertions would otherwise conclude the sheet was fully covered.
--
-- 1. THE SOLITAIRE SAVINGS UPLIFT. "6 mpd (4 card + 2 savings)", and "Lady's
--    Savings Account stays >= S$10k -- or Solitaire silently drops to 4 mpd".
--    `Cardholder` carries no savings-account balance -- the domain module
--    says why, at length: the T&C held in this corpus states 4 miles per S$1
--    and is silent on any savings uplift, so the promotion's terms are not
--    held. The 6 is asserted throughout above anyway, because 6 is what the
--    sheet claims; the 4-plus-2 decomposition is not assertable, and neither
--    is the S$10k condition. MISSING FIELD: a Lady's Savings Account balance
--    on `Cardholder`.
--
-- 2. WHICH POT A CAP FIGURE BELONGS TO -- NO LONGER A MISSING FIELD, AND
--    STILL NOT ASSERTED. Two of the sheet's claims are about pot IDENTITY
--    rather than pot size. Solitaire: "S$750 Dining + S$750 Family ... Unused
--    room in one category does NOT transfer" -- two pots that must be
--    different. Revolution: "S$1,000 online + contactless (combined)" -- two
--    channels that must share one pot. The assertions above show only that a
--    dining purchase and a grocery purchase each see S$750, and that an
--    online purchase and a tap each see S$1,000; sameness and difference are
--    a further claim.
--
--    Until 2026-09-21 this read as a missing field on `Cap`, and that is now
--    WRONG: `Cap` carries `pool`, a STRING naming which pot the transaction
--    runs against, and the domain module says in terms that it was added
--    because "the cheat sheet's claim that two pots do not transfer is only
--    checkable if the pot is named". So the claim is expressible today.
--
--    ASSERTED SINCE 2026-09-21, under "Which pot" in the stack-table section
--    above. An earlier draft of this note deferred them on the ground that
--    naming a pot the rule modules had not settled would fail on spelling.
--    That ground was sound and the conclusion did not follow: a comparison
--    between two answers of the same card names no string at all. Four
--    assertions, no rate figures: the Dining pot is one pot, the Family pot
--    is one pot, those two are not each other, and Revolution's online and
--    contactless pots are.
--
--    What remains genuinely unasserted is the SIZE claim read across pots --
--    "S$1,500 combined". The assertions say each pot admits S$750 and that
--    the pots differ, which entails it, but nothing states the total, and
--    `Cap` has no field that would.
--
-- 3. WHICH WAY THE ACQUIRER WILL FLAG IT. The sheet routes by channel --
--    "if ordered online", "contactless", "Apple Pay default" -- and its
--    figures are the figures for a transaction that lands the way the row
--    expects. Nothing in this file asserts that it does, because nothing the
--    cardholder can depose to settles it, so every fixture leaves the
--    indicator Unknown. This is NOT a missing field: the domain has the
--    field and it has an explicit `Unknown` value, and the gap is in the
--    cheat sheet, which gives the reader no way to tell a row whose rate is
--    certain from a row whose rate is a hope about someone else's acquirer.
--    That is the most useful thing this comparison can surface and it is
--    surfaced by the failures, not by an assertion.
--
-- 4. THE CASHBACK CARDS. SC Smart's "6% cashback, ~S$60/mo rebate" and DBS
--    Live Fresh have no representation at all: no `Card` constructor, and
--    `Rate answer` answers only in miles. Not a gap to be filled here -- this
--    is a miles corpus -- but it is why one whole waterfall row and three
--    second-choice cells are unasserted.
--
-- Two further things are expressible but deliberately NOT asserted. The yuu
-- unlock and the PAssion unlock are baked into `S5 the month` as met, so nothing
-- below tests what happens when they are missed. The sheet's headline rates
-- are post-unlock rates and it prints no pre-unlock figures, so there is no
-- claim to transcribe. A test of the unmet month belongs in the encoding
-- taken from the T&Cs, which is where the thresholds are actually stated.
-- And `Rate answer`'s two conditional branches, `miles per dollar if the
-- merchant flags online` and its card-present twin, are never asserted
-- against. Transcribing the sheet's figures onto the branch each row implies
-- would answer a different and narrower question -- "is the sheet right ABOUT
-- A TRANSACTION THAT LANDS THE WAY IT EXPECTS" -- and would hide the gap
-- named in (4) by assuming it away. If that comparison is wanted it should be
-- a second file, deposited under its own name, not a silent change to this
-- one.
-- ===========================================================================
